almost 60 000 people have died from  covid-19 in China in the past five weeks  that's according to new data released on  Saturday it's a huge increase from  previous figures and health officials  say the elderly has been hit the hardest  it's really ill patients are mainly  elderly people with the oldest being 105  the average age 75 and a half and those  age 60 and above accounting for 89.6  percent of the cases it's also common  for them to have a variety of underlying  diseases  the World Health Organization in several  countries have accused China of  under-representing the scale of the  outbreak  early last month Beijing abruptly lifted  its zero covert policy after almost  three years  hospitals Nationwide were overwhelmed  and medical staff under enormous  pressure including American doctor  Howard Bernstein everything was just  completely  clogged up you know the emergency room  was full every bed was full the waiting  room was full waiting and to get to the  emergency room the theater Clinic was  full and then all the ICU and hospital  beds were taken  previously only people who died from  coronavirus induced respiratory failure  were included in the official death toll  now those who died of the virus in  combination with other illnesses are  being counted the government says the  number of people being treated in Fever  clinics like these peaked in late  December but that number has now  declined by about 80 percent  Dr Bernstein says his hospital is no  longer crowded but the outbreak is far  from over  there was a sort of you know shocking  amount of illness and degree of illness  and  um and now  now we're dealing with a different  covid phenomena  which uh you know which I'm identifying  is people who are ill in December who  have still  do not feel like they've come  millions of Chinese are traveling from  cities to remote regions in the lead up  to the Lunar New Year movement that's  expected to cause a surge in infections  authorities are focusing on improving  medical facilities and access to  medicines in rural areas  International Health experts have  welcomed the new data but as the figures  only include those who died in hospital  they say the true death toll could be  much higher  training you Al Jazeera Beijing
 

